ADVISOR RELATIONSHIPS //

## Extend institutional discipline to every client—while you keep the relationship.

### Co-branded discretionary management for affiliates who need a fiduciary standard to execute, document, and report—right-sized for family portfolios of almost any size.

![Two people are sitting at a table with a third person outside the frame, engaged in conversation in a well-lit room with large windows. There are coffee mugs, potted plants, and a tablet on the table.](/images/pages/advisor-relationships/499718b990-e1b3c0fb-f87a-4584-8714-2f91399651f5.webp)

WHO IT’S FOR //

### Insurance brokers, wealth advisors, CPAs and financial planners who:

-   We have a **fiduciary standard** to trade and rebalance within a documented mandate
    
-   Want **institutional-style portfolios** adapted for everyday families—not only UHNW
    
-   Choose to **own the client relationship** while outsourcing portfolio design, execution, and reporting
    

![Three people walking and talking in a park during the late afternoon, with trees, a gazebo, and a fountain in the background.](/images/pages/advisor-relationships/28149b7769-32401592-0e3f-4ae9-b7ef-d78f8a9eaade.webp)

-   How we size & structure
    
    -   Suitability first; right-size by liquidity & risk
        
    -   Liquidity tiers (liquid, semi-liquid, select illiquid) to match cash-flow needs
        
    -   Vehicle choice based on cost, access, and tax profile
        
    
-   Due diligence & monitoring
    
    -   Manager selection framework (team, strategy, edge, risk)
        
    -   Ongoing surveillance (performance vs. drivers, drawdown behavior)
        
    -   Re-up / redeem rules; no “set-and-forget”
        
    
-   Tax & admin view
    
    -   Asset location guidance (registered vs. taxable)
        
    -   Capital calls/cash-flow mapping (where applicable)
        
    -   Simple, consolidated reporting
        
    
-   Who it’s for
    
    -   Long-horizon families open to a measured alt sleeve
        
    -   Investors wanting resilience without complexity sprawl
        
    -   Owners pre/post liquidity who need stability through transitions
        
    
-   Important notes
    
    -   Availability/minimums vary; not all strategies are appropriate for all clients.
        
    -   Past performance is not indicative of future results.
        
    

